+//! SCRATCH (never committed): M1 GraphBLAS coarsening, optimized copy (m1opt).
+//!
+//! Shared pieces of the reuse bench (`m1_reuse_bench.rs`): the level coarsening of design §3
+//! (`coarsen_level`), the hierarchy driver, graph loading, feral, and the host CSR access used by
+//! the optimized paths.
+//!
+//! Every optimization sits behind its own switch in `M1O` (comma list); the baseline is `M1O=`
+//! (empty). `M1O_BREAK=<name>` perturbs that optimization's output so the equality check fails.
+//!   usel     u = select(m == false) instead of the complemented-mask masker
+//!   zmatch   matches carried in the gather vector Z; no per-round mate assign
+//!   nowait   no per-call GrB_wait; one wait on each level's outputs
+//!   cpack    host leader numbering in one pass; C and C' packed; C*A without a transpose; w_c on
+//!            the host
+//!   caprc    cap mask by a row scale and a column scale
+//!   hcon     contraction A_c = C A C' as one host pass over A's CSR (sorted rows, no diagonal)
+//!   (the reuse-side switches are listed in m1_reuse_bench.rs)
+
